<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani rice export prices seen mixed next week.</title>
<headline>Pakistani rice export prices seen mixed next week.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani rice export prices are likely to remain mixed next week because of sluggish demand from foreign buyers, dealers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Super basmati was likely to fall on lack of demand, but IRRI-6 rice would firm on interest from the Gulf and African countries, exporter Khalid Ghori of Matco Rice Processing said.</p>
<p>Reports that the Philippines was interested in buying IRRI-6 had failed to translate into orders or inquiries with private exporters or the state-run Rice Export Corporation of Pakistan.</p>
<p>&quot;We heard a lot of news of Philippines buying but they have not yet contacted the private exporters,&quot; Ghori said.</p>
<p>Following are exporters' weekly FOB rates per tonne:</p>
<p>						 Thursday    March 6</p>
<p>    Basmati super			  $625/650    $700/715</p>
<p>    IRRI-6  (new)			  $225/235    $215/225</p>
<p>Following are domestic rates in rupees per 100 kg:</p>
<p>						 Thursday    March 6</p>
<p>    Basmati super			  2,100/2,500 2,200/2,600</p>
<p>    Basmati ordinary		     1,500/1,800 1,550/1,850</p>
<p>    IRRI-6				     680/725     680/725</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
